{
  "transcript": "Did you know falling into a black hole could turn you into spaghetti? Seriously, and not the tasty kind. Imagine falling feet first toward a smaller black hole. Gravity pulls harder on your feet than your head, so your body stretches longer, thinner, until it tears apart. Scientists call this spaghettification. But here's the creepy twist. From far away, someone would see you slow down and fade near the edge. But for you, time keeps moving. Cross the event horizon and there's no coming back. Congratulations. You went exploring the universe and became its longest noodle.",
